{"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux relies on specific patterns to ensure correct ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" behavior, efficient rendering, and safe concurrency. This article explains the reasoning behind these patterns.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"The-Snapshot-Pattern","type":"heading","text":"The Snapshot Pattern","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Store.send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" copies the observer tree into a local struct, mutates the copy via the reducer, then assigns changed properties back. This happens internally via ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxObservable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"code":"State(observer:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" packs, ","type":"text"},{"code":"State.apply(_:to:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" unpacks.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The pattern exists for two reasons:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" equality checking.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" The "},{"code":"set","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" accessor checks "},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and suppresses no-op notifications. Swift’s "},{"code":"_modify","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" accessor (used by "},{"code":"inout","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") fires notifications unconditionally. The snapshot pattern routes through "},{"code":"set","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Cross-slice observation isolation.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" The "},{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" macro generates a separate "},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" class for each "},{"code":"@Slice","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" property. A view reading "},{"code":"store.items","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" won’t re-render when only "},{"code":"store.ui","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" changes, because they live on different observer objects."}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" macro generates the observer class tree and ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxObservable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformance automatically. Hand-written conformance is still possible for advanced cases — see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxObservable","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Explicit equality guards ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"if x != state.x { x = state.x }"},{"type":"text","text":") are unnecessary. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" already checks equality on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"type":"text","text":". Unconditional assignment is safe."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Note"},{"anchor":"Dispatch-Loop-Detection","type":"heading","text":"Dispatch Loop Detection","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" warns if ","type":"text"},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is called more than 100 times per debounce interval. This usually means ","type":"text"},{"code":"send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" isn’t using the snapshot pattern, causing cascading re-renders that trigger re-dispatches.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Reducer-Weight","type":"heading","text":"Reducer Weight","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Reducers run synchronously on the MainActor. Move O(n²) work into an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and dispatch the result back as an action.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Effect-Threading","type":"heading","text":"Effect Threading","level":2},{"style":"important","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Effects run on Swift concurrency’s cooperative thread pool via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task { @concurrent in }"},{"type":"text","text":". Blocking calls ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Process.waitUntilExit()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DispatchSemaphore.wait()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Thread.sleep()"},{"type":"text","text":") hold threads hostage. If enough block, the pool starves and the MainActor freezes."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Important"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use async alternatives: ","type":"text"},{"code":"terminationHandler","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" + continuation instead of ","type":"text"},{"code":"waitUntilExit()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task.sleep()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead of ","type":"text"},{"code":"Thread.sleep()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", async file I\/O instead of ","type":"text"},{"code":"Data(contentsOf:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swi